{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments","id":1519313,"title":"Spheres as Instruments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-31T22:39:29-07:00","id":1519313,"title":"Spheres as Instruments","content":"In other threads, there has been some definite opinions expressed against the way that some effects/rotes have spheres added to them for seemingly no reason - the most prominent example, I believe, being Spirit, which even has a sidebar A Bit of Spirit? in How Do You Do That? about adding Spirit to effects just to represent their spiritual nature. &quot;What does each sphere do?&quot; some forum members ask, and rightly so.<br /> <br /> But I was thinking, what if there was some small thing that these additions did do, that could help us differentiate the style of the magic? (Which in turn helps us tell the story of the characters.) So...<br /> <br /> What if certain Spheres themselves could act as an instrument, or allow access to an instrument that would otherwise be unavailable?<br /> <br /> Take Spirit, for example. A Bit of Spirit? (if used) says that Spirit 2 is necessary to invoke spirits in order to achieve other effects. (To invoke spirits of decay to invoke an Entropy effect.) What if we just said that &quot;invoke a spirit&quot; is itself an instrument?<br /> <br /> Not that there is much in the way of firm rules around what instruments are required to produce an effect, of course. Each mage has a base of seven instruments, and gradually sets them aside one by one as Arete climbs, but they aren't directly linked to particular effects (although I would say they should be linked to a mage's particular implementation of a rote - a mage who uses Voice and Vocalizations to cast a rote should have to fall back on an improvised effect, at best, to achieve the same thing when rendered mute). There's no minimum number of instruments to be used to produce any effect. So counting use of the Spirit sphere to &quot;invoke the spirits&quot; as an instrument doesn't have a direct effect. It's really just asking the ST for a little extra leniency when evaluating whether a mage's use of instruments is good enough.<br /> <br /> And like any other instruments, there should be circumstances in which it is unavailable. If the Gauntlet is particularly thick or under the influence of an Avatar Storm, or maybe if an effect has cut an area off from the spirit world, or the like. Or maybe for some reason the spirits occasionally just say no - if you're relying on the spirits to do the work for you, you probably need to put some effort in to stay in their good graces!<br /> <br /> Also, it's probably not good enough as the only instrument to invoke a Spirit 2+ effect, at least in many cases. It is not the intent to make the use of (other) instruments redundant for Spirit 2+ effects.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I could see Mind giving access to a &quot;power of the mind&quot; instrument for psychic characters - the kind who simply think about something happening, and it does.<br /> <br /> And possibly also Life for those characters who draw on &quot;lifeforce&quot; to achieve effects - especially when using sacrifice to power an effect, so that a mage might simply draw lifeforce from a chicken directly without using a knife to cut its throat. (But no using this offensively against a target who can defend themselves - if you want an actual damaging effect, you need to cast that yourself. If you would need to roll to see if you can dispatch your sacrifice with a knife, you can't substitute use of Life sphere to perform the sacrifice.)<br /> <br /> Thoughts? I don't know myself whether I would or will use these ideas, but there might be concepts of interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T02:01:26-07:00","id":1519320,"title":"","content":"At the very least, this Instrument would be awkward when it comes to working genuine Spirit Effects. \u201cI want to Step Sideways, which is Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022 [or whatever]; so I'll use my Spirit Sphere as one of the Instruments.\u201d And Surpassing the Instrument would be especially weird under those circumstances: \u201cI've dispensed with the need for Spirit, so I'll take a \u20131 to my difficulty for using it with this Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022 Effect.\u201d<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't have a problem with \u201cA Bit of Spirit\u201d as written: if I as a player wasn't to say that my character also needs to add Spirit \u2022 or \u2022\u2022 to all of his workings that don't already involve Spirit \u2014 oh, and by the way, my character already <i>has</i> Spirit \u2022\u2022 \u2014 what's the harm? The difficulty of the casting doesn't change; there's no Quintessence cost that's charged for having a Conjunctional Effect; and since my character already has the two dots of Spirit on the character sheet, it's not like requiring him to include them in a non-Spirit Effect will limit him in any way. (And no, I don't buy that there will be situations where requiring the inclusion of Spirit \u2022\u2022 will make the casting impossible.)<br /> <br /> So from a strictly practical perspective, it strikes me as a great big \u201cmeh\u201d. I wouldn't do it, myself; but I see no harm in doing it if you want to. And I see no point in complaining about it; it simply isn't a big enough deal to worry about. <br /> <br /> From a conceptual point of view, on the other hand\u2026 the <i>heart</i> of the problem with \u201cA Bit of Spirit\u201d is that it conflates Sphere requirements with Focus requirements. And that muddied thinking has the potential to cause me to throw Spirit \u2022\u2022 into a Rote write-up when my character goes to share his magical knowledge with others. Which <i>isn't</i> appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T03:15:22-07:00","id":1519324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519320#post1519320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, this Instrument would be awkward when it comes to working genuine Spirit Effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did mention that. No using \u201cinvoke the spirits\u201d alone to achieve a Spirit 2+ effect.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s more awkward when it comes to Mind effects, really. The telekineticist who just thinks about things happening and they happen is a stable of certain genres that fit pretty well into the Technocratic worldview, and doing something like this to explain the difference between them and a hermetic mage who has to make a bunch of gestures and noises to achieve an effect the telekineticist achieves just by looking at something works pretty well\u2026 until you consider that telepathy is the baseline for such characters, and now you have Mind standing in for the gestures, when both characters have Mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519320#post1519320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a conceptual point of view, on the other hand\u2026 the <i>heart</i> of the problem with \u201cA Bit of Spirit\u201d is that it conflates Sphere requirements with Focus requirements. And that muddied thinking has the potential to cause me to throw Spirit \u2022\u2022 into a Rote write-up when my character goes to share his magical knowledge with others. Which <i>isn't</i> appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, I can see that being entirely appropriate. I think it could be very easy for characters to build stuff into rotes that really doesn\u2019t need to be there, and make it much harder for others to learn those rotes as a result. The player wants to make sharing rotes easy, but characters can mess up.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T03:20:12-07:00","id":1519325,"title":"","content":"While I don't have a problem with the concept of having Instruments that can only really be accessed with magic, it doesn't really explain why you'd add Spheres to effects. If my instrument is &quot;invoking the spirits&quot; then I just need to be able to talk to them. I could cast that effect separately go focus on building up for a larger duration, or have that ability from Backgrounds or Merits too. Adding Spheres to effects to act as Instruments just by having more dots in the effect than others might doesn't feel like it capture the idea all that well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T04:07:49-07:00","id":1519330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519325#post1519325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my instrument is &quot;invoking the spirits&quot; then I just need to be able to talk to them. I could cast that effect separately go focus on building up for a larger duration,</div> </div> </div> </div>What you\u2019re saying here is the opposite of what I described. Sure, you could spend time casting a separate effect, then go talk to the spirits, and call that conversation an instrument, but that\u2019s much more involved and roundabout. \u201cInvoking the spirits\u201d would be more like having the spirits watching out for you and helping your magic along without you having to do quite so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T14:29:12-07:00","id":1519364,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why that's &quot;round about.&quot; It's more involved in a sense, but it falls under the same basic logic of why adding Spirit 2 to effects basically doesn't mean anything anyway: it has no mechanical effect and only characters that would be invested in the Spirit Sphere in the first place would form a Focus that would use such a thing.<br /> <br /> If I'm playing a spirit-mage that deals with spirits that much as part of their Focus and mystic practice in general, I'm going to want the ability to sense and speak with spirits in some fashion so often the odds of me not having such an effect (or alternate ability) seems negligent. That's like a Hermetic that draws mystic circles going around without a writing implement handy at all times. It would be &quot;round about&quot; for a character not heavily invested in this, but it's exceedingly everyday-normal for one that is (who is the kind of mage that would be plopping Spirit into all their effects in the first place).<br /> <br /> My point is, that what you're suggesting isn't really making the Spheres potential Instruments, but rather specific effects the Spheres cover being Instruments. And if those effects are so important to a mage, they're going to be using those effects all the time (or get access to them in other ways), not just taking on some meaningless dots to a casting to represent that effect being put into the casting as an Instrument. Having the effect up separately is also very practical because it means you're taking out steps to cast quickly should the need arise, or lets you do things like rolling an Abilities Enhancing Magick check to invoke the spirits for the benefits of that.<br /> <br /> And as I said, I'm not opposed to the concept of Instruments that need magic to use, but that's not making Spheres themselves Instruments, which doesn't really solve why people don't like the idea of adding a few dots in a Sphere to lots of your effects as that sidebar proposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T00:29:31-07:00","id":1519401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519364#post1519364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why that's &quot;round about.&quot; It's more involved in a sense, but it falls under the same basic logic of why adding Spirit 2 to effects basically doesn't mean anything anyway: it has no mechanical effect and only characters that would be invested in the Spirit Sphere in the first place would form a Focus that would use such a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because \u201ceffect\u201d is a term of art in Mage: the Ascension (especially when you say \u201ccast an effect\u201d). It has a specialised meaning in the rules.<br /> <br /> And when you want to cast an effect, you need an Arete roll to see if you manage to do it, and then there\u2019s that rule about only rolling Arete once each round so you have to then delay the effect you are trying to actually achieve to the next round, and possible paradox for the instrument effect in addition to paradox for the ultimate effect\u2026<br /> <br /> As an ST, I would not want to be that mean to the player of a spirit-mage. I\u2019d rather just say that this connection to the spirit world with no real game-mechanical consequence (most of the time) is just covered by the casting roll already called for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519364#post1519364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm playing a spirit-mage that deals with spirits that much as part of their Focus and mystic practice in general, I'm going to want the ability to sense and speak with spirits in some fashion so often the odds of me not having such an effect (or alternate ability) seems negligent.</div> </div> </div> </div>And depending on what you want out of that, I may or may not require you to make Arete rolls for it. If you just want to roleplay how your character chatters with spirits nobody else is seeing pretty much all the time, I\u2019m not going to ask you to continuously roll for it. If you expect a heads-up from me when a dark spirit approaches, or the spirit world shows an ill aspect when you enter dangerous territory, or I provide useful advice relayed through the mouths of your spirit guides, I\u2019m going to want you to lay out your expectations and make an Arete roll to establish the effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T00:35:08-07:00","id":1519402,"title":"","content":"That said, if you ever do want to use one magical effect as an instrument to create another magical effect, building on top of one another in a big ritual, I\u2019m down with that. Just like if you\u2019ve got a mage whose practice involves laying out rocks in a pattern on the ground, but one day wants to produce a really big effect by laying out really big rocks in a pattern the size of Stonehenge, and lacking a handy excavator uses a telekinetic effect to move the big rocks around, I\u2019m good with that.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s just not the sort of thing I was intending to talk about in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T03:31:11-07:00","id":1519406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519401#post1519401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And when you want to cast an effect, you need an Arete roll to see if you manage to do it, and then there\u2019s that rule about only rolling Arete once each round so you have to then delay the effect you are trying to actually achieve to the next round, and possible paradox for the instrument effect in addition to paradox for the ultimate effect\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... you seem to be vastly underestimating mages here.<br /> <br /> A mage heavily invested in spirit dealings is just going to do a ritual ever six months (or less if you let them) to constantly have this up; not cast it ever turn. That's why &quot;Spirit 2 is an instrument when added to an effect that doesn't need it,&quot; doesn't really add anything to the issues people have. Mages that would benefit from that would have Spirit 2 effects active on themselves for long durations because... why not if it's that important to them?<br /> <br /> If my mage has seeing and speaking to spirits up as a near-constant effect... what does adding Spirit 2 to my effects matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And depending on what you want out of that, I may or may not require you to make Arete rolls for it. If you just want to roleplay how your character chatters with spirits nobody else is seeing pretty much all the time, I\u2019m not going to ask you to continuously roll for it. If you expect a heads-up from me when a dark spirit approaches, or the spirit world shows an ill aspect when you enter dangerous territory, or I provide useful advice relayed through the mouths of your spirit guides, I\u2019m going to want you to lay out your expectations and make an Arete roll to establish the effect. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why you cast it as a ritual in your sanctum to get a bunch of successes so it lasts for months at a time. Then you don't have to roll Awareness to justify activating it with a fresh Arete roll all the time. Once it's up, it's up until you purposefully end it, or someone tries to counter it. No constant rolling, or even rolling at dramatic moments (at least not Arete, Awareness to sense shifts in things would still be an appropriate thing anyway)... because you're a spirit mage that wants to see and talk to spirits all the time so you give yourself that ability... it's not exactly hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519402#post1519402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that\u2019s just not the sort of thing I was intending to talk about in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... what do you want to talk about? You seem to be focusing a trying to find anything besides critiques of your original idea to try to argue against, rather than taking the feedback and trying to refine your concept in response to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T05:05:53-07:00","id":1519410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519406#post1519406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... you seem to be vastly underestimating mages here.<br /> <br /> A mage heavily invested in spirit dealings is just going to do a ritual ever six months (or less if you let them) to constantly have this up; not cast it ever turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you\u2019re vastly overestimating mages here. I\u2019m fully aware that the setting has some powerful mages who are capable of pulling off some big things, but not every mage is like that. We\u2019re talking PCs here.<br /> <br /> A lot of starting PCs will have Arete 2. They can\u2019t have more than Arete 3, and some have Arete 1. Some won\u2019t have a Sanctum at all.<br /> <br /> A duration of 6 months requires at least 6 successes. A mage with Arete 1 and no Sanctum may be able to establish such an effect, but I\u2019m not going to assume they all will. There\u2019s a significant chance that such a mage will fail if they try, and that failure can bring consequences. I\u2019m not going to assume that every mage is walking around with always-active effects.<br /> <br /> And I don\u2019t think my players are coming with that assumption either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T05:51:41-07:00","id":1519413,"title":"","content":"I see lots of reasons to *not* do that and no reason at all to do it.<br /> <br /> First, it is against the raw of how magick mechanics works from all Mage editions. If you follow the step-by-step, you will see that you shouldn't add spheres due to instruments used, only to what the effects does. So, your effect result needs Sipirt sphere?<br /> <br /> If you want to levitate something you might use Correspondence or Forces. You want to summon a spirit and the spirit will use a charm to levitate the thinf for you? Use spirit.<br /> <br /> If you are not interacting *mechanically* with spirits, but your mage inatrument in-game interacts with spirits, you don't need that sphere.<br /> <br /> Second, if you start adding spheres like that, you should end up needing other spheres for every effect. Hdydt do that with Mind but it fails to that with othera spheres.<br /> For example, you should need Life to use any instrument involving your body. Forces for every instrument involving energy and forces. And why not Matter for ...practically every instrument that has an object? To me, all of this is bullshit and makes pattern sphere superior to the others.<br /> <br /> Third, players could abuse that to get -1 Arete difficulty by sneaking in their affinity sphere. Of course, they can try to do that without that crazy rule, but with it you would get the -1 diff in every effect. As a ST I would ask for the player to have an explanation on the result of the spell (and not the instruments) to allow sneaking in a sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, why use this rule? I just can't think of a single good regson for it. Mage gives you the freedom to add any fluff you want in your instruments. You want to use spirits? Ok. You want to use the power of your mind? Sure. You cast spells by using Chi? No problem. You don't need any sphere to any of those instruments, just... use the instruments. It's fluff.<br /> <br /> The reason hdydt made that rule was to bloat effects and make it harder to use some instruments. Do you really think that is needed? You really want to make it harder to players that want to use Chi?<br /> <br /> So, I ask again. Why do that?<br /> <br /> PS: note that some effects will need other s\u00e7heres by raw. Example: you want to create fire from &quot;nothing&quot;. If you use quint as fuel, you need Forces+Prime. If you want to literally use your mind energy, you need Forces+Mind and there would be consequences (maybe headache or smt). This is raw, regardless of your instrument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 08-02-2023, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T08:15:19-07:00","id":1519430,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: \u201cA Bit of Spirit\u201d doesn't make it harder to use Instruments. In practice, it doesn't even make it harder to work Effects; because the mages using A Bit of Spirit of variations thereof will have the one or two dots that it requires. The worst I can say about the rule in practical terms is that it does nothing useful; the best I can say about it in practical terms is that it does nothing harmful. In practical terms, it <i>does nothing</i>. Which is why, in practical terms, my response to it is \u201cwhatever\u201d. It's only in theoretical terms that there are issues. <br /> <br /> The \u201cSpheres as Instruments\u201d hack being suggested here has the potential to go the same way; and in my humble opinion, that would be the best case scenario. But as Lord Revan just pointed out, it has the potential to do harm to gameplay. You would need to add a caveat that Spheres can only be Standard Instruments, never Personalized or Unique, in order to avoid abusive loopholes in the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:36:43-07:00","id":1519506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519410#post1519410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you\u2019re vastly overestimating mages here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Lots of people might not have done as much deep diving as some of us on the forum (and plenty of other places) have done over the years to know exactly what mages - even starting level mages - are really capable of, but that's not the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of starting PCs will have Arete 2. They can\u2019t have more than Arete 3, and some have Arete 1. Some won\u2019t have a Sanctum at all. </div> </div> </div>I thought you didn't want to talk about all this? Why are you avoiding the core question (&quot;If my mage has seeing and speaking to spirits up as a near-constant effect... what does adding Spirit 2 to my effects matter?), since your idea isn't just for starting level characters, but for all characters.<br /> <br /> That said:<br /> <br /> I mentioned Sanctum just to skip over a bunch of things with a common mage Background to have at least some dots in: Sanctums get around coincidental vs. vulgar debates, and provide a bonus to ritual casting that ensures you'll be at the minimum difficulty of 3 combined with the implied safety and lack of external pressures.<br /> <br /> But since we're apparently discussing this more fully: Under HAP, it's coincidental because you're not doing anything a Sleeper could actually perceive. They can't see that you can see spirits, and they can't hear that your voice can cross the Gauntlet. After your ritual, you just look like a normal person and nothing about you is noticeably different to anyone without magical senses.<br /> <br /> Arete 1: irrelevant, it's a Spirit 2 effect.<br /> <br /> Arete 2: It's a coincidental effect (base diff 5), Finding a net -2 Difficulty should be painfully easy as you're doing this in downtime. No negative modifiers should be coming up. You're already doing this as an extended roll ritual for a long duration, so setting aside some extra time is easily done. Using your personal instrument. Being near a Node (you don't have to own it). Etc. So we're rolling at diff 3. That's an average of 1.4 success a roll, not great since there's decent odds of failing rolls (botching is very rare though). Fortunately it's downtime and you can afford to drop some WP to bring it up to 2.4 average successes and drop your failure rate to 3%. So three rolls, 3 WP, and boom, 6 month effect in the bag. Simple.<br /> <br /> Arete 3: Everything with Arete 2, but more dice so better rolls. Also, you qualify for the Automatic Success rules at ST discretion (even if for some reason the core book addressing this for magical casting forgets that you can lower difficulties in how it's written), and can roll a maximum of 8 single success rolls... more than you need to get off the effect without the risks of rolling.<br /> <br /> Your spirit focused mage finding two days a year to set aside for some deep ritual practices to keep up their connections to the outer worlds is not hard for them to do. At Arete 2 they might want to set aside a bit more time to recover from the mentally draining activity, but that's why mages love to cast these sorts of things as long duration effects during downtime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019m not going to assume that every mage is walking around with always-active effects. </div> </div> </div>At Arete 2 (Arete 1 is playing the game on hard-mode anyway)? Without house-rules or personal player reasons to go against the incentives of the systems, most mages should have a small number of effects that tend to just have on for extended periods of time because they're too useful to not have if casting in-the-moment would make casting really hard to do effectively. You don't want too many, because that's a path towards casting difficulties as described in the books, but a few key effects is definitely worth it.<br /> <br /> Preparation is one of a mage's strongest allies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I don\u2019t think my players are coming with that assumption either. </div> </div> </div>OK. But the books say what the books say. The incentives are what they are. I've been playing the game long enough where I do things like make Arete 1 mages for the challenge of it, because I know how much it's hobbling my character's ability to actually do much magic. I play with friends where are assumptions are to use the Golden Rule to use house rules to make the game more rewarding for what it says its supposed to do, rather than what it actually says to do.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't change what mages are actually capable of when people that know how the game works put their minds to something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T20:37:25-07:00","id":1519557,"title":"","content":"I don't care to devote big chunks of time to arguing over this (maybe lots of time in aggregate, eventually... but better in small pieces rather than lots at once) so I'm going to just pull out a few small pieces of things and question assumptions one by one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519413#post1519413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, if you start adding spheres like that, you should end up needing other spheres for every effect. Hdydt do that with Mind but it fails to that with othera spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? What tells us that any rule we care to make has to be the same for all spheres?<br /> <br /> HDYDT has some specific tweaks for Mind in order to emulate particular archetypes that are staples of certain genres. A Little Bit of Spirit is likewise targetting particular archetypes, as are the odd additions of spheres to particular effects (in some cases - I think some others are probably just plain wrong). Are there equivalent archetypes for Matter that would be represented<br /> <br /> I mean, if a mage's practice involves manipulation of a physical instrument that cannot be achieved through the use of the mage's hands, I could probably be persuaded to consider allowing that mage to add Matter to their effects to build in the manipulation of that instrument at no further cost. I don't really see a problem with that. I'd be willing to listen to a player, when running a game.<br /> <br /> But I question the idea that doing something with these spheres <i>requires</i> doing the same with other spheres. Why does it have to be that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T23:10:24-07:00","id":1519563,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, the problem is that it's leaning into something that goes against the core point of the design of the game (which some people like because it's also adding flavor).<br /> <br /> Mage's magic system is supposed to be flexible enough where any effect you can think of is possible. It's also supposed to be flexible enough that wildly different styles of magic can all use it coherently. When a mage wants to summon a fireball out of nothing and blast someone with it, it's a Forces 3/Prime 2 effect. It's that for a Hermetic using an incantation of flames, an Etherite firing flame-gun, or an Akashic pulling an anime style fire attack on someone. All of those differences in approach are what M20 combined into the Focus concept. Focus is what's supposed to change between different mages that do things differently. The Spheres to pull off an effect are supposed to be the same (as clarified by M20 stating firmly that it's a PBD system).<br /> <br /> When Focus starts changing what Spheres are needed to pull off an effect, it's moving away from the idea of the magic system working the same for everyone on a mechanical level. When you remove that barrier, you take away any reason to say some Spheres should be able to act this way, while other's can't. Sure, you don't have to let people do it, but it just comes off as being arbitrary and controlling to say that my reality hacker can't add Forces to everything to manipulate the electronic code of the universe, while Mind gets to do more to make psychic-Focus character feel more mechanically special. You've eliminated any rational argument against making it the same for all Spheres..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T00:49:28-07:00","id":1519570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519413#post1519413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, players could abuse that to get -1 Arete difficulty by sneaking in their affinity sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so, on abuse of instruments... The rules say that mages start with at least 7 instruments, one of which is personalized, and which can be set aside, one by one, from Arete 3 upwards. However, there's nothing to say how many of these instruments are required to produce any effect, nor how the use of those seven instruments is distributed among the effects that the mage uses. <br /> <br /> So there's nothing in the rules to stop a player saying, &quot;My character's Arete is 3, and his instruments are a personalized wand, and six backup wands. Every effect is produced by pointing a wand, and what I want to happen, happens. And I've set aside my personalized wand, so I can get all of my effects to happen without pointing it, and if I do point my personalized wand at something I get -1 difficulty to the roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> But if I player says that to me, I know he's taking the mickey.<br /> <br /> Now, there's really good reasons why these rules are as loose as they are. They need to be able to handle an extraordinarily broad range of approaches to magic. Some mages should have an instrument that is locked in a wall safe and gets brought out once in the campaign for some special event. Some should have a go-to instrument that provides most of their day-to-day effects. That's fine, but if I'm running the game, it's up to me to negotiate the use of these instruments with the players, to maintain balance between characters, and balance against the rest of the world, and provide for good stories.<br /> <br /> So if I have players I can't negotiate this with, and who are looking for ways to trick me into stuff that is problematic, I'm already in trouble. And frankly, if I have a player like that, I'm more inclined to suggest that they are not compatible with the game I intend to run.<br /> <br /> (And I have successfully run systems that are far more structured than this part of MtA, and others far less structured than this part of MtA.)<br /> <br /> Now, I get that some of you want to play MtA in a style that expects players to be hunting for an angle, and you want rules that provide less opportunity for players to pull off a trick that you don't see coming. And that's fine. I'm not suggesting that every game should adopt something like I proposed at the start of this thread. And I've had some contact with the Camarilla/WW Fan Club/Beyond the Sunset, so yeah, I'm aware that not every group is going to play nice.<br /> <br /> But maybe not everything that is discussed and considered has to come from that very defensive position. It's not all groups that are like that.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to let a player link every effect to a sphere, call it an instrument, claim that instrument has then been set aside, and get -1 difficulty on everything. It's really easy to just point out that this approach doesn't really make sense, and isn't really good for the story. I'd be willing to listen to a player who thinks otherwise, but I find it hard to see this tool being set aside until most or all other tools have been set aside.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T01:40:07-07:00","id":1519574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519563#post1519563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, you don't have to let people do it, but it just comes off as being arbitrary and controlling to say that my reality hacker can't add Forces to everything to manipulate the electronic code of the universe, while Mind gets to do more to make psychic-Focus character feel more mechanically special.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t get it. What does this reality hacker think they are missing out on? The psychic character isn\u2019t getting to roll any extra dice, and their difficulties aren\u2019t being lowered. So what precisely is the player of the reality hacker bothered about?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T03:12:43-07:00","id":1519586,"title":"","content":"The ability to use the Sphere they want to use &quot;as an Instrument&quot; instead of the &quot;certain Spheres&quot; you've arbitrarily decided should be allowed to do so (and yes, you said &quot;certain Spheres&quot; in your opening post), for whatever your house rule ends up allowing.<br /> <br /> Though I still don't get what you actually want to talk about, because you keep trying to debate the smallest nitpicks and ignore big questions that are hanging in this thread for you to address.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T16:44:05-07:00","id":1519677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519570#post1519570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, there's really good reasons why these rules are as loose as they are. They need to be able to handle an extraordinarily broad range of approaches to magic. Some mages should have an instrument that is locked in a wall safe and gets brought out once in the campaign for some special event. Some should have a go-to instrument that provides most of their day-to-day effects. That's fine, but if I'm running the game, it's up to me to negotiate the use of these instruments with the players, to maintain balance between characters, and balance against the rest of the world, and provide for good stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>The M:tA rules for Foci and Instruments also need to handle to variety and sheer power and intensity of the various categories of Magick Spells and Effects. The player of a M:tA protagonist - including when for example a lady who is a Technocrat would be portrayed - has a need and benefits from clear direction in regard to how each type of Magick ( or Inspired Science ) is developed, learned, used, and perfected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T19:35:39-07:00","id":1519698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519586#post1519586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ability to use the Sphere they want to use &quot;as an Instrument&quot; instead of the &quot;certain Spheres&quot; you've arbitrarily decided should be allowed to do so (and yes, you said &quot;certain Spheres&quot; in your opening post), for whatever your house rule ends up allowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, no concrete objection, just a vague worry that I (or another ST) might negotiate unfairly with my players. That\u2019s way too vague for me to consider it further,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519586#post1519586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I still don't get what you actually want to talk about, because you keep trying to debate the smallest nitpicks and ignore big questions that are hanging in this thread for you to address.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your tone is demanding, but nobody, myself included, is obliged to address anything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T20:31:27-07:00","id":1519704,"title":"","content":"And now, for the sake of comparison, I\u2019m going to take a brief look at the rules that HDYDT gives for the sorts of characters in question. From page 35 onwards\u2026<br /> <br /> For a psychic elementalist (telekineticist and similar, presumably including characters like Eleven from Stranger Things and Carrie from Carrie and similar examples):<ul><li>Add Mind 3 to the pattern for relevant effects; no problem for the character who already has Mind 3, but may in some cases increase (never decrease) the difficulty of the associated Arete roll (if 3 is higher than any other sphere in the pattern).</li> <li>The option to spend Willpower for an automatic success on the Arete roll\u2026 which was already an option, as far as I can tell. This is identical to the standard use of Willpower.</li> <li>Make an additional Willpower roll in order to move objects, control fire, or create objects.</li> <li>Optionally (on the part of the ST) spend a temporary Willpower point in order to move large objects (telekinesis).</li> <li>Spend a temporary Willpower point in order to create solid objects.</li> </ul>These are all downsides for the psychic elementalist. There is no mechanical advantage at all to playing this type of character, as far as I can see.<br /> <br /> For the spiritual elementalist, I think you can make an argument that the rules under Telekinesis, Pyrokinesis, and Psychomanifestation are not intended to apply. That would leave these changes:<ul><li>Add Spirit 2 to the pattern for relevant effects; no problem for the character who already has Spirit 2, but may in some (rare) cases increase (never decrease) the difficulty of the associated Arete roll (if all other spheres in the pattern are at 1).</li> <li>The option to spend Willpower for an automatic success on the Arete roll\u2026 which was already an option, as far as I can tell. This is identical to the standard use of Willpower.</li> </ul>The downside here is much smaller, but it\u2019s still all downside. If you do think the rules under the subheadings apply, the downsides get more serious.<br /> <br /> In no case does a character of these types get an advantage.<br /> <br /> Under this approach, playing a telekineticist would just suck. I would hate to have a player say they have a cool idea for a telekineticist, and have to tell them that they get extra chances to fail, but still have to make mystic gestures or use a physical tool (just like the regular spellcasters - and something that doesn\u2019t fit a telekineticist\u2019s concept well), and get no compensatory advantages at all, however minor. (If I had decided to play a telekineticist myself, and an ST told me that, I might not be worried about the mechanical disadvantages. After all, I once played a mute character in a system with no compensation for disability just to see how well I could roleplay using my body alone. I\u2019m not often worried about having a disadvantaged character. But I may be worried about the poor modelling of telekinesis.)<br /> <br /> So the published method of dealing with these characters is not great, and the prevailing opinion in this forum seems to be that the published method sucks.<br /> <br /> Which leads me to wonder, how would others handle a request to play a telekineticist? What instruments do you allow for them, and how do you balance that against the character who needs his hands free to gesticulate, and the other character who needs to manipulate an object? Or do you just allow some forms of magick to be easier to access than others?<br /> \u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T01:59:42-07:00","id":1519715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519704#post1519704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are all downsides for the psychic elementalist. There is no mechanical advantage at all to playing this type of character, as far as I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely some upsides and advantages - maybe also extra rules and merits - could be included for protagonists and characters of this category. It is not described or mentioned that this approach and method in regard to Spells and Effects is troublesome, inefficient, or problematic.<br /> <br /> Psychic ( or psionic ) elementalism seems to be an interesting, characterful, and sensible.<br /> Methods, philosophies, and approaches that are unique and distinct in background and story can often definitely and clearly carry and justify at least some particular tuned rules and notable advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T03:19:28-07:00","id":1519725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519698#post1519698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, no concrete objection, just a vague worry that I (or another ST) might negotiate unfairly with my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Some Spheres get this and others don't for no explained reason,&quot; is in fact, a concrete objection. Way to deflect again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your tone is demanding, but nobody, myself included, is obliged to address anything. </div> </div> </div>It's text, tone is mostly what you make up in your head when you read my words.<br /> <br /> Besides that, let's go back to your words: &quot;But that\u2019s just not the sort of thing I was intending to talk about in this thread.&quot; To which you seem to be lying, because you keep talking about &quot;the sort of thing&quot; you didn't intend for the thread, and refuse to explain what you do want to talk about.<br /> <br /> I'd rather come off as demanding than how sound in my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519704#post1519704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which leads me to wonder, how would others handle a request to play a telekineticist?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hand them Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Mages are free to be specialize, or just only cast effects they want to cast out of personal preference, but a character who's whole deal is moving things with their minds is why we have sorcerers as playable characters instead. That's the splat for characters that are hyper-specialized in how their powers works.<br /> <br /> If a player wants to make a mage that started thinking of their powers as psychic abilities and is expanding to the true power of a will-worker, the Book of Secrets added a bunch of extra Focus material; and specifically the Psionics Practice, which associated Paradigms and Instruments. It's a fine guide for a player that wants a mage with a psychic inspired Focus, who can then pick Spheres that do the kinds of effects they want to be able to do (so, take Forces if you want to levitate stuff like any other mage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T06:22:50-07:00","id":1519738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519570#post1519570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so, on abuse of instruments... The rules say that mages start with at least 7 instruments, one of which is personalized, and which can be set aside, one by one, from Arete 3 upwards. However, there's nothing to say how many of these instruments are required to produce any effect, nor how the use of those seven instruments is distributed among the effects that the mage uses.<br /> <br /> So there's nothing in the rules to stop a player saying, &quot;My character's Arete is 3, and his instruments are a personalized wand, and six backup wands. Every effect is produced by pointing a wand, and what I want to happen, happens. And I've set aside my personalized wand, so I can get all of my effects to happen without pointing it, and if I do point my personalized wand at something I get -1 difficulty to the roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> But if I player says that to me, I know he's taking the mickey.<br /> <br /> Now, there's really good reasons why these rules are as loose as they are. They need to be able to handle an extraordinarily broad range of approaches to magic. Some mages should have an instrument that is locked in a wall safe and gets brought out once in the campaign for some special event. Some should have a go-to instrument that provides most of their day-to-day effects. That's fine, but if I'm running the game, it's up to me to negotiate the use of these instruments with the players, to maintain balance between characters, and balance against the rest of the world, and provide for good stories.<br /> <br /> So if I have players I can't negotiate this with, and who are looking for ways to trick me into stuff that is problematic, I'm already in trouble. And frankly, if I have a player like that, I'm more inclined to suggest that they are not compatible with the game I intend to run.<br /> <br /> (And I have successfully run systems that are far more structured than this part of MtA, and others far less structured than this part of MtA.)<br /> <br /> Now, I get that some of you want to play MtA in a style that expects players to be hunting for an angle, and you want rules that provide less opportunity for players to pull off a trick that you don't see coming. And that's fine. I'm not suggesting that every game should adopt something like I proposed at the start of this thread. And I've had some contact with the Camarilla/WW Fan Club/Beyond the Sunset, so yeah, I'm aware that not every group is going to play nice.<br /> <br /> But maybe not everything that is discussed and considered has to come from that very defensive position. It's not all groups that are like that.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to let a player link every effect to a sphere, call it an instrument, claim that instrument has then been set aside, and get -1 difficulty on everything. It's really easy to just point out that this approach doesn't really make sense, and isn't really good for the story. I'd be willing to listen to a player who thinks otherwise, but I find it hard to see this tool being set aside until most or all other tools have been set aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you cant have 7 wands as your 7 instruments. Wands is <b>one</b> instrument (if your mage uses several wands or only one, is up to you, but it counts as 1 of the 7 either way).<br /> <br /> Yes, you can go and use the dropped instrument for the -1 diff, but you have to provide an explanation about why that instrument was able to cast such spell. And that's ok.<br /> <br /> My point is not only that players will attempt to sneak their affinity sphere, but that they wont even need to sneak it in!!!<br /> you already did that when you added Mind into every godamn effect.<br /> <br /> Want to throw a fireball? Mind 3+Forces 3+Prime 2<br /> Want to levitate shit? Mind 3+Forces 2<br /> <br /> So, the mage gets Mind as affinity sphere and practically all of his effects get automatically -1 diff.<br /> <br /> The same for Chi (the most ridiculous thing Hdydt did)<br /> <br /> Chi push: Forces 2+Prime 2 <b>and</b>1 quint (instead of only Forces 2 as it should be)<br /> Cho flight: Forces 2+Life 2+Prime 2 <b>and</b> 1 quint (instead of only Forces 2 as it should be)<br /> Chi healing: Life 2(or 3 for others)+Prime 2 <b>and</b> 1 quint per health level (instead of only Life 2-3)<br /> <br /> I will save you the work and go ahead and tell you that they added Prime 2 and 1 quint for every effect, even the most basic ones, just beacause &quot;chi&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, for the reasons I am completely against this.<br /> <b>It is not how the mechanics of the game works or ever worked.</b><br /> <br /> <b>I see no reason at all to do that</b><br /> <br /> Also, it is <b>not</b> presented as an optional rule. So if you want to play a martial artist mage, you need to have Prime 2 and spend quint in simple and dumb effects, like healing, when other mages with other paradigm do not. Foci should not influence mechanics this way.<br /> <br /> If my ST follow that rule I had only two options: make a mage with the exact same foci but with a different explanation (I'm a martial artist that uses energy, but it's not chi) or I don't play in that table at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just a final request, could you answer my question: why do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 08-04-2023, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T20:16:02-07:00","id":1519923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519738#post1519738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you cant have 7 wands as your 7 instruments. Wands is <b>one</b> instrument (if your mage uses several wands or only one, is up to you, but it counts as 1 of the 7 either way).</div> </div> </div> </div>The rulebook doesn\u2019t explicitly say that. It gives the even more broad category of \u201cWands, Rods, and Staves\u201d, but that\u2019s only an example of an instrument.<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t allow seven individual wands as seven different instruments because we know the intent of the rules is to allow us to build reasonable characters, and as STs we negotiate that outcome with the players.<br /> <br /> (Not that it would matter anyway, if the intent of the player is to never use any instrument except the one that grants a mechanical bonus. We can get more abusive than six extra individual wands.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519738#post1519738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the mage gets Mind as affinity sphere and practically all of his effects get automatically -1 diff.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he doesn\u2019t. There is no such modifier. It\u2019s not a personalised instrument, it\u2019s not a unique instrument, and it hasn\u2019t been transcended. I was explicit in my original post that the only advantage provided by this type of instrument is some leeway on what they have to do to enact relevant effects, and if I wasn\u2019t explicit enough then I\u2019m being so now.<br /> <br /> If you intend to be helpful, feel free to point out a rule that would provide a -1 difficulty that you think I have missed. You should be aware, though, that I\u2019m about 95% certain that my response will simply be, \u201cThat doesn\u2019t sound like it should apply to this case, so it doesn\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519738#post1519738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a final request, could you answer my question: why do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>To better emulate certain types of characters, and the feats we see them doing in fiction, that seem like a good fit for the setting but not well-supported by the rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T06:30:27-07:00","id":1520100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519923#post1519923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rulebook doesn\u2019t explicitly say that. It gives the even more broad category of \u201cWands, Rods, and Staves\u201d, but that\u2019s only an example of an instrument.<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t allow seven individual wands as seven different instruments because we know the intent of the rules is to allow us to build reasonable characters, and as STs we negotiate that outcome with the players.<br /> <br /> (Not that it would matter anyway, if the intent of the player is to never use any instrument except the one that grants a mechanical bonus. We can get more abusive than six extra individual wands.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it says that you have to choose 7 instruments. Choosing the same instrument 7 times it's on the highest level of min/max (insert over 9000 meme) and we have nothing pointing that it should be allowed. But yeah, that's not the core of the discussion, so we can drop this. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519923#post1519923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, he doesn\u2019t. There is no such modifier. It\u2019s not a personalised instrument, it\u2019s not a unique instrument, and it hasn\u2019t been transcended. I was explicit in my original post that the only advantage provided by this type of instrument is some leeway on what they have to do to enact relevant effects, and if I wasn\u2019t explicit enough then I\u2019m being so now.<br /> <br /> If you intend to be helpful, feel free to point out a rule that would provide a -1 difficulty that you think I have missed. You should be aware, though, that I\u2019m about 95% certain that my response will simply be, \u201cThat doesn\u2019t sound like it should apply to this case, so it doesn\u2019t.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>All it takes is the player to chooae his sphere instrument as his personalized one. If you treat spheres as instruments and the player can choose any instrument to be personalized, why not the sphere?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1519923#post1519923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To better emulate certain types of characters, and the feats we see them doing in fiction, that seem like a good fit for the setting but not well-supported by the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very well supported by the rules. You just take psionics for the telekinesia guy. And martial arts for the chi guy. And you work your explanations and foci, to explain how his cast his effects. There is absolutely no need to add this house rule. Those characters can be emulated as much as any other.<br /> <br /> Of course, one could add this house rule (or any other) at their table, but personally, I would not play at it.<br /> If you make it optional, and not a rule as hdydt did, I can see this working. Improving players options is good. Restricting or penalizing them with rules that go against every single Mage core book is bad (see my Chi example from hdydt in my last post).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T07:03:40-07:00","id":1520105,"title":"","content":"I have recently purchased a STV product called <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/446015\" target=\"_blank\">Prism of Focus</a> by <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Charles%20Siegel\" target=\"_blank\">Charles Siegel</a>, one of my favorite STV authors. This book deals primarily with clarifying and expanding on the Focus system, such as breaking Paradigms up into Tenets that more precisely target specific topics that a Paradigm ought to address; and the bulk of the book takes more detailed examinations of various Practices, supplementing the official descriptions with Common Resonance Traits, a Benefit and Penalty, a selection of Rotes and Wonders emblematic of that Practice, Paradox Effects, Seekings, and occasionally specialized variants practiced by particular Traditions, Conventions, or Crafts. <br /> <br /> The main relevance to this thread is found on page 113, under the special Benefit provided by the Dreamspeaker Specialty of Shamanism, called <i>Spirit Ties</i>: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By adding the \u201cbit of Spirit\u201d as per the Sidebar in <b>How Do You DO That?</b> p. 16, a Dreamspeaker changes the difficulty of their effects to be based on the Gauntlet rather than the usual rules based on Highest Sphere and Vulgarity. </div> </div> </div>In short, it changes \u201cA Bit of Spirit\u201d from a do-nothing rule to something that, in the right hands, actually does something <i>useful</i>. And it does this through the Focus system, though not by making the Spirit Sphere an Instrument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T02:45:13-07:00","id":1520176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520100#post1520100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All it takes is the player to chooae his sphere instrument as his personalized one. If you treat spheres as instruments and the player can choose any instrument to be personalized, why not the sphere?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Because I say so. We are dealing with house rules here. If we want to use a house rule, and we need it to not interact in a certain way with the base rules in order to avoid problems, we can just make it so. I want to dispel the notion that anybody else can force a house rule to work a particular way in other people\u2019s games just because you want to argue against the idea.<br /> <br /> 2. Because personalized/personal (the rulebook uses both these words, apparently interchangeably) instruments must be personalized/personal. Look at the examples of personalized instruments: a lucky baseball bat; a rowan wand; a hand-built guitar; a gift of whiskey, three cigars and a virgin rooster. These are all more specifically tailored for the mage than the standard instruments. There\u2019s only the mutagenic cocktail of chemicals that someone could argue is a bunch of chemicals that were generic but become mutagenic as part of casting the effect, but I don\u2019t believe that was the author\u2019s intent. You\u2019ve made no attempt to explain how this instrument is being personalized, and I\u2019m saying I would want a better explanation than what I anticipate someone coming up with. Especially if we\u2019re talking about the \u201cpower of the mind\u201d case; you\u2019ve personalized the power of your own mind? More than other mages? I doubt it.<br /> <br /> 3. Because the M20 rulebook does not say <b>any</b> instrument can be personalized anyway. It says to pick a personal instrument. There\u2019s nothing saying that all of the standard instruments can be personalized. As a player, you still need to negotiate with the ST, and be reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520100#post1520100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is very well supported by the rules. You just take psionics for the telekinesia guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. So, our psionicist is escaping from the secret lab run by the government. We see him (emulating a TV show here, so I\u2019ll reference sight and shots) running down a hall lit by fluorescent lights. Suddenly, two soldiers come around the corner at the end of the hall. Their rifles start to come up to point at our fleeing hero. The camera gives a close-up of the psionicist\u2019s eye, and the soldiers fly backwards, slamming into the wall. They slump to the ground, and the psionicist runs past them, turning down the corridor they came from, before they can recover.<br /> <br /> What instrument did this character use?<br /> <br /> From the Psionics practice\u2019s list of instruments: it\u2019s certainly not bodywork, brain/computer interface, devices and machines, nanotech, cards and instruments of chance, dances and movement, drugs, fashion, formulae and math, numbers and numerology, group rites, music, languages, management and HR, sex and sensuality, symbols, True Names, voice and vocalisations, writings, inscriptions, or runes. These are all observably not present in the scenario.<br /> <br /> Eye contact, based on the classic eye close-up? Not really, meeting the gaze of the psionicist is really not necessary in the genre to get thrown across the room.<br /> <br /> Energy, because this seems to involve the production of kinetic energy? No, the energy instrument is about doing something to manipulate existing energy in order to produce an effect. If kinetic energy is involved here, it\u2019s the result of the effect.<br /> <br /> Meditation? The last one left in the list. But is this quiet reflection? Screening out distractions? Does it sound like the use of something that \u201cdoesn\u2019t work well [\u2026] in high-stress situations\u201d?<br /> <br /> So what\u2019s the appropriate instrument? People here keep saying that the rules cover it, but you won\u2019t say precisely how you think the rules cover it.<br /> <br /> And so far, I find what I see in the rules for this particular case unconvincing. It\u2019s like trying to run the Earthsea setting with D&amp;D. Fans of the system have said it\u2019s good enough since before the first edition of Mage: the Ascension was published, but mere assertion doesn\u2019t convince everyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520100#post1520100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you make it optional, and not a rule as hdydt did, I can see this working. Improving players options is good. Restricting or penalizing them with rules that go against every single Mage core book is bad (see my Chi example from hdydt in my last post).</div> </div> </div> </div>An option for the player? Sure. That\u2019s all I ever suggested. If a player wants to do a psionicist or a spiritualist without using this new type of instrument on offer (if I ever offer it at all) I have no problem with that. (Of course, it\u2019s then on the player to tell me what instrument their character is using in an example like the one above. And I have to find it convincing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T02:54:04-07:00","id":1520177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520105#post1520105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have recently purchased a STV product called <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/446015\" target=\"_blank\">Prism of Focus</a> by <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Charles%20Siegel\" target=\"_blank\">Charles Siegel</a>, one of my favorite STV authors. This book deals primarily with clarifying and expanding on the Focus system, such as breaking Paradigms up into Tenets that more precisely target specific topics that a Paradigm ought to address; and the bulk of the book takes more detailed examinations of various Practices, supplementing the official descriptions with Common Resonance Traits, a Benefit and Penalty, a selection of Rotes and Wonders emblematic of that Practice, Paradox Effects, Seekings, and occasionally specialized variants practiced by particular Traditions, Conventions, or Crafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like this might be worth a look anyway, even if I don\u2019t like the actual implementation of its ideas. Just giving players some direction on how to build their own unique practices may be of benefit. Thanks for the tip.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure I would want to replace the standard difficulty calculations with something eise entirely, but I guess a lot would depend on the specifics of the implementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T05:06:16-07:00","id":1520185,"title":"","content":"Like I said, the idea is to give some sort of benefit to adding Spirit \u2022\u2022 to the Effect, so that it's not just flavor. <br /> <br /> The existing rules <i>already</i> allow Spirit Magick to replace the standard difficulty calculations with something else entirely; see M20 p.544, <i>Spirit Magick and the Gauntlet</i>: <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u2022 Spirit Effects cast against someone on the same side of the Gauntlet have a difficulty based on the highest Sphere + the usual <i>coincidental</i>, <i>vulgar</i>, or <i>vulgar with witnesses</i> modifiers.<br /> \u2022 To cast Spirit Effects across the Gauntlet, check the <b><i>Gauntlet Ratings chart</i></b> to find the difficulty of your spell.</div>This just leverages that rule by saying that the mage who uses <i>A Bit of Spirit</i> is working the Effect with the cooperation of spirits on the other side of the Gauntlet, and that they're doing much of the \u201cheavy lifting\u201d for working the Effect; so the Effect counts as \u201ccrossing the Gauntlet\u201d even if it normally wouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T05:27:48-07:00","id":1520187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520176#post1520176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Because I say so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. As ST of your table you can do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520176#post1520176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. So, our psionicist is escaping from the secret lab run by the government. We see him (emulating a TV show here, so I\u2019ll reference sight and shots) running down a hall lit by fluorescent lights. Suddenly, two soldiers come around the corner at the end of the hall. Their rifles start to come up to point at our fleeing hero. The camera gives a close-up of the psionicist\u2019s eye, and the soldiers fly backwards, slamming into the wall. They slump to the ground, and the psionicist runs past them, turning down the corridor they came from, before they can recover.<br /> <br /> What instrument did this character use?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you just can't be that shallow with paradigm. A real character has to explain how he think Reality works and how he do magick. This means a well built Paradigm, with practices and instruments wraping everything together. You can't just pick instruments and that's all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520176#post1520176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the Psionics practice\u2019s list of instruments: it\u2019s certainly not bodywork, brain/computer interface, devices and machines, nanotech, cards and instruments of chance, dances and movement, drugs, fashion, formulae and math, numbers and numerology, group rites, music, languages, management and HR, sex and sensuality, symbols, True Names, voice and vocalisations, writings, inscriptions, or runes. These are all observably not present in the scenario.<br /> <br /> Eye contact, based on the classic eye close-up? Not really, meeting the gaze of the psionicist is really not necessary in the genre to get thrown across the room.<br /> <br /> Energy, because this seems to involve the production of kinetic energy? No, the energy instrument is about doing something to manipulate existing energy in order to produce an effect. If kinetic energy is involved here, it\u2019s the result of the effect.<br /> <br /> Meditation? The last one left in the list. But is this quiet reflection? Screening out distractions? Does it sound like the use of something that \u201cdoesn\u2019t work well [\u2026] in high-stress situations\u201d?<br /> <br /> So what\u2019s the appropriate instrument? People here keep saying that the rules cover it, but you won\u2019t say precisely how you think the rules cover it.<br /> <br /> And so far, I find what I see in the rules for this particular case unconvincing. It\u2019s like trying to run the Earthsea setting with D&amp;D. Fans of the system have said it\u2019s good enough since before the first edition of Mage: the Ascension was published, but mere assertion doesn\u2019t convince everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several instruments that could fit here, but again, you need the full foci to make a case. Having said that, I could see psionics foci in your example as being: Thought Forms, Meditation, Eye contact, Energy, Gestures, Voice, Nanotech even math.<br /> <br /> Now, the explanation will depend on the full foci:<br /> <br /> - Meditation doesn't require sitting in a lotus position with your eyes closed. You can meditate while running if you want. However, as a ST, you could ask for a roll in stressfull situations. In your example, the mage just succeded in the roll.<br /> <br /> - Eye contact arguably doesn't require eye-to-eye contact. The psionic gaze could be enough to start an effect.<br /> <br /> - Gestures is the classic one. Practically every telekinesis user do that Jedi hand waving. That would be the one I'd choose.<br /> <br /> - Energy could be the use of the psionics internal energy, and doesn't have to be an existent real life physics energy<br /> <br /> - Thoght forms are similar to meditation in a way and might not require any physical action.<br /> <br /> - If your psionic is tech based, having nanobots in his body, or some device in his brain, nanotech or any other technological instrment could fit (devices and machines)<br /> <br /> Note: I believe instrtuments works better when combined, so you could go the energy+meditation+gestures: The psionics focus his gaze into the soldiers and with a wave of his hand, he channels his energy into a burst of force.<br /> <br /> <b>Again, WHY and HOW the instruments works is a question the player has to answer, and that's what foci (pradigm, practices and instruments) is for </b>. You are right to not let players just go &quot;I'm a psionic so I dont have to do shit to cast spells&quot;. Make them explain everything,<br /> <br /> Now, what reay [b]don't[b] fit into that is the use of Mind as an instrument. Wtf this even means? The psionic look at the soldiers and...use the sphere as an instrument? How is that explained? How does that fit with the mage paradigm?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520176#post1520176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An option for the player? Sure. That\u2019s all I ever suggested. If a player wants to do a psionicist or a spiritualist without using this new type of instrument on offer (if I ever offer it at all) I have no problem with that. (Of course, it\u2019s then on the player to tell me what instrument their character is using in an example like the one above. And I have to find it convincing.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, my main issue with hdydt is that it isn't even an optional rule. Chi mages gets a <b>lot</b> of drawbacks for no reason at all. So, being an option you give to players can do no harm, I guess. If everyone is ok with that, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T05:41:52-07:00","id":1520188,"title":"","content":"I suggested a possible solution for Chi Magick in another thread: say that adding Prime \u2022\u2022 to an Effect and spending a point of Quintessence to make it a Chi Effect basically lets you <i>combine</i> the Effect with an otherwise-mundane task: rather than \u201cAbilities Enhancing Magick\u201d or \u201cMagick Enhancing Abilities\u201d, make it \u201cAbilities <i>as</i> Magick\u201d, and roll Arete+Ability instead of Arete on the one hand, or Attribute+Ability on the other. Chi Flight would be Arete+Athletics; Chi Healing would be Arete+Medicine; Chi Shout would be Arete+Intimidation; and so on. <br /> <br /> It's a potentially massive boost; but on the other hand, having to spend a Quintessence on <i>each use</i> is a potentially massive <i>cost</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T07:24:09-07:00","id":1520193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520187#post1520187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, you just can't be that shallow with paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>For describing a single feat in a single scene, I sure can. Let\u2019s not pretend that I was claiming that this describes an entire character (including paradigm). For the purpose of the example, that was fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520187#post1520187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Meditation doesn't require sitting in a lotus position with your eyes closed. You can meditate while running if you want. However, as a ST, you could ask for a roll in stressfull situations. In your example, the mage just succeded in the roll.<br /> <br /> - Eye contact arguably doesn't require eye-to-eye contact. The psionic gaze could be enough to start an effect.<br /> <br /> - Gestures is the classic one. Practically every telekinesis user do that Jedi hand waving. That would be the one I'd choose.<br /> <br /> - Energy could be the use of the psionics internal energy, and doesn't have to be an existent real life physics energy<br /> <br /> - Thoght forms are similar to meditation in a way and might not require any physical action.<br /> <br /> - If your psionic is tech based, having nanobots in his body, or some device in his brain, nanotech or any other technological instrment could fit (devices and machines)</div> </div> </div> </div>Every one of these requires either ignoring the description of that instrument, or changing what the character does in that scene. There are many examples of telekinetic characters who do not routinely use the \u201cJedi hand waving\u201d, and even many who do are shown to not need it when their hands are restrained or occupied.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520187#post1520187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: I believe instrtuments works better when combined,</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that again there is absolutely no system support for this. (My solution here is to require use of more instruments when performing more powerful effects, but that doesn\u2019t help us with the low end of the scale.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520187#post1520187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Again, WHY and HOW the instruments works is a question the player has to answer, and that's what foci (pradigm, practices and instruments) is for </b>. You are right to not let players just go &quot;I'm a psionic so I dont have to do shit to cast spells&quot;. Make them explain everything,</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the psionic character doesn\u2019t have to do shit to cast an effect, as long as the player can speak eloquently. It doesn\u2019t even matter if the explanation is convincing, because they\u2019ve spoken some words and that\u2019s the end of it. <br /> <br /> This is something I explicitly do not want. I have been roleplaying for over 30 years. I have known so many roleplayers who can string together words in a fashion that lets the listener get carried away on the sound of their voice. By now, that is incredibly boring to me. (And I\u2019ve seen too many players screw over other players in PVP LARP environments just through being able to speak more prettily.)<br /> <br /> What I want is for players to make meaningful decisions, and for those decisions to have consequences. If a player doesn\u2019t have a good explanation for an effect on the spot, I would much rather support them so that we can make one together. But on the other hand, if a player eloquently explains why today their use of magic sidesteps the limitations they have previously chosen for their practice, I\u2019m going to say no.<br /> <br /> So if your psionicist relies on Jedi hand gestures, that means he\u2019s stuck when his hands are restrained. (Build a psionicist who can either use the gesture or meditate? Sure. If your hands are restrained but you have time, meditate. If you have no time but your hands are free, gesture. If you have neither, be stuck.)<br /> <br /> And then we come back to the psionicist who thinks it, and it happens\u2026 and the need for at least some consequence for when they are standing alongside the mystic ritualist.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m aware that there are those who just want to hear some words from the players, but telling those who want decisions, consequences, and equitable negotiation that you are happy with eloquence alone is not helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520187#post1520187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, what reay [b]don't[b] fit into that is the use of Mind as an instrument. Wtf this even means? The psionic look at the soldiers and...use the sphere as an instrument? How is that explained? How does that fit with the mage paradigm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go back and read my original post. Stop getting hung up on the thread title. There was a single paragraph that explicitly mentioned Mind. Read it, note that it does not contain the phrase \u201cMind as an instrument\u201d, and think this over from the start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520187#post1520187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my main issue with hdydt is that it isn't even an optional rule. Chi mages gets a <b>lot</b> of drawbacks for no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t care what your issues with HDTDT\u2019s chi magic are. You\u2019re the one who keeps bringing that up. It\u2019s utterly unrelated to anything I have talked about. There\u2019s a reason I just keep deleting every mention you make of chi when I reply. It is irrelevant, and after this one paragraph pointing out that it is irrelevant I intend to go back to ignoring it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T09:03:28-07:00","id":1520208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520193#post1520193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For describing a single feat in a single scene, I sure can. Let\u2019s not pretend that I was claiming that this describes an entire character (including paradigm). For the purpose of the example, that was fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, when you only describes the instruments used, you make it look like the mage isn't doing nothing at all. You have to provide a full foci explanation to see that there is something going on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520193#post1520193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every one of these requires either ignoring the description of that instrument, or changing what the character does in that scene. There are many examples of telekinetic characters who do not routinely use the \u201cJedi hand waving\u201d, and even many who do are shown to not need it when their hands are restrained or occupied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, then ignore gestures. But there are several instruments that do not require a physical action at all. That's why you need to describe paradigm and pratice. And I haven't changed the instruments description, the book is only a guide, you are not restriced by what is written there exactly. Some instrments are poorly described (liek energy) with a single paragraph, you can develop further.You aren't even restriced by the list of instruments there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520193#post1520193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the psionic character doesn\u2019t have to do shit to cast an effect, as long as the player can speak eloquently. It doesn\u2019t even matter if the explanation is convincing, because they\u2019ve spoken some words and that\u2019s the end of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, psionics is not willworking. Again, several instruments do not require physical actions and someone looking from outside might think they aren't doing anything. The truth is, there is always something going on. As a ST, you have to ask for the foci explanation and if they can't give a plausible one, you can deny. Your example of &quot;the psionics look and magick is done&quot; is not acceptable by itself. It needs a deeper explanation involving foci for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520193#post1520193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I explicitly do not want. I have been roleplaying for over 30 years. I have known so many roleplayers who can string together words in a fashion that lets the listener get carried away on the sound of their voice. By now, that is incredibly boring to me. (And I\u2019ve seen too many players screw over other players in PVP LARP environments just through being able to speak more prettily.)<br /> <br /> What I want is for players to make meaningful decisions, and for those decisions to have consequences. If a player doesn\u2019t have a good explanation for an effect on the spot, I would much rather support them so that we can make one together. But on the other hand, if a player eloquently explains why today their use of magic sidesteps the limitations they have previously chosen for their practice, I\u2019m going to say no.<br /> <br /> So if your psionicist relies on Jedi hand gestures, that means he\u2019s stuck when his hands are restrained. (Build a psionicist who can either use the gesture or meditate? Sure. If your hands are restrained but you have time, meditate. If you have no time but your hands are free, gesture. If you have neither, be stuck.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, every instrument have at least some drawback. Some more than other. meditation and thought forms doesnt require a specific physical action, it all happens inside the mage's mind. A lab, on the other hand, have a much bigger drawback.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520193#post1520193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then we come back to the psionicist who thinks it, and it happens\u2026 and the need for at least some consequence for when they are standing alongside the mystic ritualist.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m aware that there are those who just want to hear some words from the players, but telling those who want decisions, consequences, and equitable negotiation that you are happy with eloquence alone is not helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here is the problem. Psionics aren't only about &quot;I think and it happens&quot;. There are a lot of things going on. Depending on the paradigm, I could see the ST requiring concentration rolls for stressful situations if the psionics is using meditation, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520193#post1520193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go back and read my original post. Stop getting hung up on the thread title. There was a single paragraph that explicitly mentioned Mind. Read it, note that it does not contain the phrase \u201cMind as an instrument\u201d, and think this over from the start.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t care what your issues with HDTDT\u2019s chi magic are. You\u2019re the one who keeps bringing that up. It\u2019s utterly unrelated to anything I have talked about. There\u2019s a reason I just keep deleting every mention you make of chi when I reply. It is irrelevant, and after this one paragraph pointing out that it is irrelevant I intend to go back to ignoring it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>OP description of using Mind is <br /> <br /> &quot;Similarly, I could see Mind giving access to a &quot;power of the mind&quot; instrument for psychic characters - the kind who simply think about something happening, and it does.&quot;<br /> <br /> How does this works? What is happening? Why thinking about something change reality? You are ignoring the fact that you have to create a paradigm and conect it with instruments through practices and instead is just shoving a sphere there. That works against the mechanics of the game and do not help into developing the RP aspect. When you fully describe your entire foci, you will see that you are trying to solve a problem that you created when you didn't go deeper in foci, and doing it in a bad way (by changing raw mehanics).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T22:32:53-07:00","id":1520263,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520208#post1520208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, when you only describes the instruments used, you make it look like the mage isn't doing nothing at all. You have to provide a full foci explanation to see that there is something going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you keep assuming that I won\u2019t do that at the appropriate time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520208#post1520208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnd I haven't changed the instruments description,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you have. Your use of several of those instruments is altered from what is given in the book.<br /> <br /> That isn\u2019t a problem, not on its own. (It potentially could be, if you make changes that lead to unfair results for your players, but that requires much more context to evaluate.) But don\u2019t make changes from the rulebook and then try to tell others the rules are perfect as-is and need no changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520208#post1520208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't even restriced by the list of instruments there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It\u2019s almost like the intent is to allow STs or even players (with the approval of their ST for their final character build) to make up new stuff when they find that the existing stuff doesn\u2019t fit what they are after. You know, like I did.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520208#post1520208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, several instruments do not require physical actions and someone looking from outside might think they aren't doing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Fashion is an excellent example of such. Wear the clothes, and you have a tool already in use without doing anything further (which doesn\u2019t mean that this single instrument alone is necessarily enough to produce all effects the mage has spheres for\u2026 but it may be enough for something). But that doesn\u2019t automatically make every instrument with no associated physical action balanced in the context of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520208#post1520208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The truth is, there is always something going on. As a ST, you have to ask for the foci explanation and if they can't give a plausible one, you can deny. Your example of &quot;the psionics look and magick is done&quot; is not acceptable by itself. It needs a deeper explanation involving foci for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me be clear: I, as an ST, am satisfied that plausible enough explanations for the type of psionicist, who can achieve the type of feat, that I gave as an example to exist in the setting of M:tA. It is not your place to tell me that such characters do not have a deep enough explanation, because you are not an ST for any character I intend to play.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, the character is fine. Mechanically, I find system support lacking.<br /> <br /> And you haven\u2019t given me any reason to change my mind. You\u2019ve told me to reject the character if I find the explanation lacking, but l don\u2019t find the explanation lacking, and that isn\u2019t the problem in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520208#post1520208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, every instrument have at least some drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you made one up, when you suggested that meditation involves a concentration roll. The usual drawback of the meditation instrument is that it can\u2019t be used quickly, under pressure, and on the move. But you wanted something that could be used quickly, under pressure, and on the move, so you made up a new drawback. In doing so, you effectively made up a new instrument, too. (And you did it without laying out a character\u2019s complete paradigm.)<br /> <br /> Now, I\u2019m not so satisfied with that particular drawback. The reason why doesn\u2019t matter right now. Even if I was satisfied with that drawback, what if I\u2019ve got a player who isn\u2019t?<br /> <br /> I made up an instrument, and gave it a drawback. I see potential to use it for a case where I\u2019m dissatisfied with what the rulebook gives. I\u2019ve said nothing about forcing every psionicist to use it. If a player wants to make a psionicist character without it, and I\u2019m satisfied with the instruments they choose instead, that\u2019s fine.<br /> <br /> Each of these instruments is just another tool in the toolbox we have for building characters.<br /> <br /> And frankly, the great bulk of HDYDT is the same - examples of how you could build things, but without a requirement that absolutely every character work that way. And yet you are so bonkers over it that you\u2019ve been railing against stuff in there in multiple threads where it isn\u2019t even relevant. Just take a step back, and take a breath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520208#post1520208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP description of using Mind is<br /> <br /> &quot;Similarly, I could see Mind giving access to a &quot;power of the mind&quot; instrument for psychic characters - the kind who simply think about something happening, and it does.&quot;<br /> <br /> How does this works? What is happening? Why thinking about something change reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>How does meditation change reality? How does performing a dance or a kata change reality? How does wearing ceremonial robes change reality?<br /> <br /> You\u2019re not trying to attack existing instruments from the book by insisting that they only ever be discussed in the context of a complete focus. You aren\u2019t doing it for your own new ideas that aren\u2019t in the book. Stop doing that for other ideas that aren\u2019t in the book.<br /> <br /> Just like with any other instrument, there are multiple possible justifications for this to work. Basically any justification that would work for the standard meditation instrument, or your modified meditation instrument with a concentration roll, will work for this instrument too. Stop trying to pretend that it\u2019s so different on that front. If you need one to get your head around it, pick one from among the ones you used to consider meditation with a concentration check.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520208#post1520208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are ignoring the fact that you have to create a paradigm and conect it with instruments through practices and instead is just shoving a sphere there.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I\u2019m not. I\u2019m consigning that work to a later character creation session, with actual players, and not wasting my time trying to detail the multiple different complete paradigms an idea might be used in, in order to gain approval from an ST I will never play any of them under, in a forum format that isn\u2019t particularly suited to those kind of negotiations. Just like you did, when you wrote \u201cDepending on the paradigm\u201d instead of detailing all of the paradigms that might refer to.<br /> <br /> What I am doing here is examining a new possibility for certain new instruments that may be of use when later we build characters, paradigms, and foci. If you\u2019re not interested in that type of discussion, you\u2019re welcome to just not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T03:49:53-07:00","id":1520281,"title":"","content":"You posted it on a discussion forum, and people are trying to discuss your idea with you, and you're not engaging with what people are saying. At all.<br /> <br /> You can just not. Go get a blog to post your house rules on without anyone being able to comment if you want to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T07:30:18-07:00","id":1520294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And you keep assuming that I won\u2019t do that at the appropriate time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying that you did not provide it in this thread so ppl can analyze the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you have. Your use of several of those instruments is altered from what is given in the book.<br /> That isn\u2019t a problem, not on its own. (It potentially could be, if you make changes that lead to unfair results for your players, but that requires much more context to evaluate.) But don\u2019t make changes from the rulebook and then try to tell others the rules are perfect as-is and need no changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me exactly what change I have made. Extrapolation is different than change. You *have* to develop things further than they are described in those 1 or 2 paragraph of descriptions in M20, if you care for RP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. It\u2019s almost like the intent is to allow STs or even players (with the approval of their ST for their final character build) to make up new stuff when they find that the existing stuff doesn\u2019t fit what they are after. You know, like I did.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you changed the mechanics, and a big one. That's way different than choosing other instruments out of the book list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Fashion is an excellent example of such. Wear the clothes, and you have a tool already in use without doing anything further (which doesn\u2019t mean that this single instrument alone is necessarily enough to produce all effects the mage has spheres for\u2026 but it may be enough for something). But that doesn\u2019t automatically make every instrument with no associated physical action balanced in the context of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have I ever said instruments were (or should) be balanced? You are not reading my posts. I even used the lab example. No, instruments, like several things in WoD are not balanced and that's ok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me be clear: I, as an ST, am satisfied that plausible enough explanations for the type of psionicist, who can achieve the type of feat, that I gave as an example to exist in the setting of M:tA. It is not your place to tell me that such characters do not have a deep enough explanation, because you are not an ST for any character I intend to play.<br /> Conceptually, the character is fine. Mechanically, I find system support lacking.<br /> And you haven\u2019t given me any reason to change my mind. You\u2019ve told me to reject the character if I find the explanation lacking, but l don\u2019t find the explanation lacking, and that isn\u2019t the problem in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you are not making any fkg sense. You posted a shallow example of an effect and asked (and I quote):<br /> <br /> &quot;What instrument did this character use?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, I don't fkg know, your player has to provide this information. And you have to give it to us so we can give our opinion about it, isn't that what the forum is for?<br /> So, yeah, it is my place to tell you that you didn't provide enough info for the discussion to flow.<br /> <br /> Also, if you are ok with the player explanation, wtf do you want more?<br /> It seems that you are not worried with the RP and logical aspect of the foci (as you made it sound), but the mechanical, &quot;unbalanced&quot; aspect.<br /> Well, again, instruments are not balanced. If the player already provided an explanation that you accepted (which I hope isn't &quot;I think and then magick happens&quot;), then you are good to go. So what it doesn't have as big drawback as lab? Meditation, voice, prayers, thought forms: all of those have very little drawbacks when you compare to labs or celestial alignment.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, those instruments tend to be more vulgar than tech. That's the mechanical difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you made one up, when you suggested that meditation involves a concentration roll. The usual drawback of the meditation instrument is that it can\u2019t be used quickly, under pressure, and on the move. But you wanted something that could be used quickly, under pressure, and on the move, so you made up a new drawback. In doing so, you effectively made up a new instrument, too. (And you did it without laying out a character\u2019s complete paradigm.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wtf? Are you telling me that I created a new meditation instrument? Lol.<br /> First, it is raw that you can ask for an ability roll that are related to a foci. So, you can ask for a meditation roll for the use of meditation, if the situation is stressful. You can ask for technology roll for devices and machines if you think it's appropriate. And you can ask for esoterica rolls for several mystic instruments.<br /> Second, if you don't want to ask for a roll, just apply the &quot;mage is distracted&quot; Arete penalty of +1 to +3 that is in M20<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I\u2019m not so satisfied with that particular drawback. The reason why doesn\u2019t matter right now. Even if I was satisfied with that drawback, what if I\u2019ve got a player who isn\u2019t?<br /> I made up an instrument, and gave it a drawback. I see potential to use it for a case where I\u2019m dissatisfied with what the rulebook gives. I\u2019ve said nothing about forcing every psionicist to use it. If a player wants to make a psionicist character without it, and I\u2019m satisfied with the instruments they choose instead, that\u2019s fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't created a new instrument, you created a house rule that change the mechanics of the game. Instruments are not determined by what the effect does, but how the mage does it.<br /> If you are not forcing them, then they could use the raw for Psionics and I don't know what you want with this thread. You want to know if it's a good idea? Imho it is not and if I were a player, I would stick with the default rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each of these instruments is just another tool in the toolbox we have for building characters.<br /> And frankly, the great bulk of HDYDT is the same - examples of how you could build things, but without a requirement that absolutely every character work that way. And yet you are so bonkers over it that you\u2019ve been railing against stuff in there in multiple threads where it isn\u2019t even relevant. Just take a step back, and take a breath.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, hdydt present to us as how things work. Of course a ST can (and should) ignore Chi rules, but for all intents, it\u2019s raw and not optional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does meditation change reality? How does performing a dance or a kata change reality? How does wearing ceremonial robes change reality?<br /> You\u2019re not trying to attack existing instruments from the book by insisting that they only ever be discussed in the context of a complete focus. You aren\u2019t doing it for your own new ideas that aren\u2019t in the book. Stop doing that for other ideas that aren\u2019t in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven\u2019t provided any idea that isn\u2019t in the book. And it\u2019s your job (your player\u2019s job) to provide the explanation, not mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like with any other instrument, there are multiple possible justifications for this to work. Basically any justification that would work for the standard meditation instrument, or your modified meditation instrument with a concentration roll, will work for this instrument too. Stop trying to pretend that it\u2019s so different on that front. If you need one to get your head around it, pick one from among the ones you used to consider meditation with a concentration check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good! Then you don\u2019t need that terrible house rule at all. Just use meditation. Problem solved.<br /> I have already answered the \u201cmeditation roll&quot; issue above in this post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I\u2019m not. I\u2019m consigning that work to a later character creation session, with actual players, and not wasting my time trying to detail the multiple different complete paradigms an idea might be used in, in order to gain approval from an ST I will never play any of them under, in a forum format that isn\u2019t particularly suited to those kind of negotiations. Just like you did, when you wrote \u201cDepending on the paradigm\u201d instead of detailing all of the paradigms that might refer to.<br /> What I am doing here is examining a new possibility for certain new instruments that may be of use when later we build characters, paradigms, and foci. If you\u2019re not interested in that type of discussion, you\u2019re welcome to just not.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as we have seen, you are not worried with the RP aspect, so ok, go on without describing the full foci further, since it\u2019s not a problem to you.<br /> <br /> To sumarize:<br /> <br /> 1) You can use meditation and several other instruments with psionics with raw for what you want<br /> <br /> 2) They have, arguably, easier drawbacks. Instruments aren\u2019t balanced at all<br /> <br /> 3) If you want to add drawback to this player, use the raw skill roll for difficult situations or add +1 to +3 diff (as per M20 p.506)<br /> <br /> So yeah, no need for that house-rule at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T07:32:43-07:00","id":1520295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And you keep assuming that I won\u2019t do that at the appropriate time.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, I'm saying that you did not provide it in this thread so ppl can analyze the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, you have. Your use of several of those instruments is altered from what is given in the book.<br /> That isn\u2019t a problem, not on its own. (It potentially could be, if you make changes that lead to unfair results for your players, but that requires much more context to evaluate.) But don\u2019t make changes from the rulebook and then try to tell others the rules are perfect as-is and need no changes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Tell me exactly what change I have made. Extrapolation is different than change. You *have* to develop things further than they are described in those 1 or 2 paragraph of descriptions in M20, if you care for RP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah. It\u2019s almost like the intent is to allow STs or even players (with the approval of their ST for their final character build) to make up new stuff when they find that the existing stuff doesn\u2019t fit what they are after. You know, like I did.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, you changed the mechanics, and a big one. That's way different than choosing other instruments out of the book list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure. Fashion is an excellent example of such. Wear the clothes, and you have a tool already in use without doing anything further (which doesn\u2019t mean that this single instrument alone is necessarily enough to produce all effects the mage has spheres for\u2026 but it may be enough for something). But that doesn\u2019t automatically make every instrument with no associated physical action balanced in the context of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Have I ever said instruments were (or should) be balanced? You are not reading my posts. I even used the lab example. No, instruments, like several things in WoD are not balanced and that's ok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Let me be clear: I, as an ST, am satisfied that plausible enough explanations for the type of psionicist, who can achieve the type of feat, that I gave as an example to exist in the setting of M:tA. It is not your place to tell me that such characters do not have a deep enough explanation, because you are not an ST for any character I intend to play.<br /> Conceptually, the character is fine. Mechanically, I find system support lacking.<br /> And you haven\u2019t given me any reason to change my mind. You\u2019ve told me to reject the character if I find the explanation lacking, but l don\u2019t find the explanation lacking, and that isn\u2019t the problem in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div> Now you are not making any fkg sense. You posted a shallow example of an effect and asked (and I quote):<br /> <br /> &quot;What instrument did this character use?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, I don't fkg know, your player has to provide this information. And you have to give it to us so we can give our opinion about it, isn't that what the forum is for?<br /> So, yeah, it is my place to tell you that you didn't provide enough info for the discussion to flow.<br /> <br /> Also, if you are ok with the player explanation, wtf do you want more?<br /> It seems that you are not worried with the RP and logical aspect of the foci (as you made it sound), but the mechanical, &quot;unbalanced&quot; aspect.<br /> Well, again, instruments are not balanced. If the player already provided an explanation that you accepted (which I hope isn't &quot;I think and then magick happens&quot;), then you are good to go. So what it doesn't have as big drawback as lab? Meditation, voice, prayers, thought forms: all of those have very little drawbacks when you compare to labs or celestial alignment.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, those instruments tend to be more vulgar than tech. That's the mechanical difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And you made one up, when you suggested that meditation involves a concentration roll. The usual drawback of the meditation instrument is that it can\u2019t be used quickly, under pressure, and on the move. But you wanted something that could be used quickly, under pressure, and on the move, so you made up a new drawback. In doing so, you effectively made up a new instrument, too. (And you did it without laying out a character\u2019s complete paradigm.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Wtf? Are you telling me that I created a new meditation instrument? Lol.<br /> First, it is raw that you can ask for an ability roll that are related to a foci. So, you can ask for a meditation roll for the use of meditation, if the situation is stressful. You can ask for technology roll for devices and machines if you think it's appropriate. And you can ask for esoterica rolls for several mystic instruments.<br /> Second, if you don't want to ask for a roll, just apply the &quot;mage is distracted&quot; Arete penalty of +1 to +3 that is in M20<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now, I\u2019m not so satisfied with that particular drawback. The reason why doesn\u2019t matter right now. Even if I was satisfied with that drawback, what if I\u2019ve got a player who isn\u2019t?<br /> I made up an instrument, and gave it a drawback. I see potential to use it for a case where I\u2019m dissatisfied with what the rulebook gives. I\u2019ve said nothing about forcing every psionicist to use it. If a player wants to make a psionicist character without it, and I\u2019m satisfied with the instruments they choose instead, that\u2019s fine.</div> </div> </div> </div> You didn't created a new instrument, you created a house rule that change the mechanics of the game. Instruments are not determined by what the effect does, but how the mage does it.<br /> If you are not forcing them, then they could use the raw for Psionics and I don't know what you want with this thread. You want to know if it's a good idea? Imho it is not and if I were a player, I would stick with the default rules.<br /> <br /> <di