e":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T07:45:49-07:00","id":1520296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you keep assuming that I won\u2019t do that at the appropriate time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I'm saying that you did not provide it in this thread so ppl can analyze the situation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you have. Your use of several of those instruments is altered from what is given in the book.<br /> That isn\u2019t a problem, not on its own. (It potentially could be, if you make changes that lead to unfair results for your players, but that requires much more context to evaluate.) But don\u2019t make changes from the rulebook and then try to tell others the rules are perfect as-is and need no changes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tell me exactly what change I have made. Extrapolation is different than change. You *have* to develop things further than they are described in those 1 or 2 paragraph of descriptions in M20, if you care for RP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. It\u2019s almost like the intent is to allow STs or even players (with the approval of their ST for their final character build) to make up new stuff when they find that the existing stuff doesn\u2019t fit what they are after. You know, like I did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, you changed the mechanics, and a big one. That's way different than choosing other instruments out of the book list.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Fashion is an excellent example of such. Wear the clothes, and you have a tool already in use without doing anything further (which doesn\u2019t mean that this single instrument alone is necessarily enough to produce all effects the mage has spheres for\u2026 but it may be enough for something). But that doesn\u2019t automatically make every instrument with no associated physical action balanced in the context of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have I ever said instruments were (or should) be balanced? You are not reading my posts. I even used the lab example. No, instruments, like several things in WoD are not balanced and that's ok.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me be clear: I, as an ST, am satisfied that plausible enough explanations for the type of psionicist, who can achieve the type of feat, that I gave as an example to exist in the setting of M:tA. It is not your place to tell me that such characters do not have a deep enough explanation, because you are not an ST for any character I intend to play.<br /> Conceptually, the character is fine. Mechanically, I find system support lacking.<br /> And you haven\u2019t given me any reason to change my mind. You\u2019ve told me to reject the character if I find the explanation lacking, but l don\u2019t find the explanation lacking, and that isn\u2019t the problem in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now you are not making any fkg sense. You posted a shallow example of an effect and asked (and I quote):<br /> <br /> &quot;What instrument did this character use?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, I don't fkg know, your player has to provide this information. And you have to give it to us so we can give our opinion about it, isn't that what the forum is for?<br /> So, yeah, it is my place to tell you that you didn't provide enough info for the discussion to flow.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if you are ok with the player explanation, wtf do you want more?<br /> It seems that you are not worried with the RP and logical aspect of the foci (as you made it sound), but the mechanical, &quot;unbalanced&quot; aspect.<br /> Well, again, instruments are not balanced. If the player already provided an explanation that you accepted (which I hope isn't &quot;I think and then magick happens&quot;), then you are good to go. So what it doesn't have as big drawback as lab? Meditation, voice, prayers, thought forms: all of those have very little drawbacks when you compare to labs or celestial alignment.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, those instruments tend to be more vulgar than tech. That's the mechanical difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you made one up, when you suggested that meditation involves a concentration roll. The usual drawback of the meditation instrument is that it can\u2019t be used quickly, under pressure, and on the move. But you wanted something that could be used quickly, under pressure, and on the move, so you made up a new drawback. In doing so, you effectively made up a new instrument, too. (And you did it without laying out a character\u2019s complete paradigm.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wtf? Are you telling me that I created a new meditation instrument? Lol.<br /> First, it is raw that you can ask for an ability roll that are related to a foci. So, you can ask for a meditation roll for the use of meditation, if the situation is stressful. You can ask for technology roll for devices and machines if you think it's appropriate. And you can ask for esoterica rolls for several mystic instruments.<br /> Second, if you don't want to ask for a roll, just apply the &quot;mage is distracted&quot; Arete penalty of +1 to +3 that is in M20<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I\u2019m not so satisfied with that particular drawback. The reason why doesn\u2019t matter right now. Even if I was satisfied with that drawback, what if I\u2019ve got a player who isn\u2019t?<br /> I made up an instrument, and gave it a drawback. I see potential to use it for a case where I\u2019m dissatisfied with what the rulebook gives. I\u2019ve said nothing about forcing every psionicist to use it. If a player wants to make a psionicist character without it, and I\u2019m satisfied with the instruments they choose instead, that\u2019s fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You didn't created a new instrument, you created a house rule that change the mechanics of the game. Instruments are not determined by what the effect does, but how the mage does it.<br /> If you are not forcing them, then they could use the raw for Psionics and I don't know what you want with this thread. You want to know if it's a good idea? Imho it is not and if I were a player, I would stick with the default rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each of these instruments is just another tool in the toolbox we have for building characters.<br /> And frankly, the great bulk of HDYDT is the same - examples of how you could build things, but without a requirement that absolutely every character work that way. And yet you are so bonkers over it that you\u2019ve been railing against stuff in there in multiple threads where it isn\u2019t even relevant. Just take a step back, and take a breath.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, hdydt present to us as how things work. Of course a ST can (and should) ignore Chi rules, but for all intents, it\u2019s raw and not optional.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does meditation change reality? How does performing a dance or a kata change reality? How does wearing ceremonial robes change reality?<br /> You\u2019re not trying to attack existing instruments from the book by insisting that they only ever be discussed in the context of a complete focus. You aren\u2019t doing it for your own new ideas that aren\u2019t in the book. Stop doing that for other ideas that aren\u2019t in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I haven\u2019t provided any idea that isn\u2019t in the book. And it\u2019s your job (your player\u2019s job) to provide the explanation, not mine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like with any other instrument, there are multiple possible justifications for this to work. Basically any justification that would work for the standard meditation instrument, or your modified meditation instrument with a concentration roll, will work for this instrument too. Stop trying to pretend that it\u2019s so different on that front. If you need one to get your head around it, pick one from among the ones you used to consider meditation with a concentration check.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, good! Then you don\u2019t need that terrible house rule at all. Just use meditation. Problem solved.<br /> I have already answered the \u201cmeditation roll&quot; issue above in this post.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520263#post1520263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I\u2019m not. I\u2019m consigning that work to a later character creation session, with actual players, and not wasting my time trying to detail the multiple different complete paradigms an idea might be used in, in order to gain approval from an ST I will never play any of them under, in a forum format that isn\u2019t particularly suited to those kind of negotiations. Just like you did, when you wrote \u201cDepending on the paradigm\u201d instead of detailing all of the paradigms that might refer to.<br /> What I am doing here is examining a new possibility for certain new instruments that may be of use when later we build characters, paradigms, and foci. If you\u2019re not interested in that type of discussion, you\u2019re welcome to just not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And as we have seen, you are not worried with the RP aspect, so ok, go on without describing the full foci further, since it\u2019s not a problem to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> To sumarize:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) You can use meditation and several other instruments with psionics with raw for what you want<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) They have, arguably, easier drawbacks. Instruments aren\u2019t balanced at all<br /> <br /> <br /> 3) If you want to add drawback to this player, use the raw skill roll for difficult situations or add +1 to +3 diff (as per M20 p.506)<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, no need for that house-rule at all.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T17:12:06-07:00","id":1520910,"title":"","content":"Obviously I haven\u2019t had time for this argument in something like a week, so let\u2019s cut down to really essential bits.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520296#post1520296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, it is raw that you can ask for an ability roll that are related to a foci.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where? If it\u2019s \u201crules as written\u201d, where is it written? Because I haven\u2019t found it in the M20 core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T07:54:40-07:00","id":1520943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520910#post1520910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously I haven\u2019t had time for this argument in something like a week, so let\u2019s cut down to really essential bits.<br /> <br /> Where? If it\u2019s \u201crules as written\u201d, where is it written? Because I haven\u2019t found it in the M20 core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, the raw is that the mage has to have at least the same amount of dots in the related ability as the Sphere of the effect.<br /> it is also raw that you can apply penalties for casting and distractions are on the table in M20 p506<br /> It is also raw that a mage can roll his relates ability to reduce casting difficulties.<br /> <br /> So, add everything together and in a stressful situation you apply a penalty on the Arete roll diff. And the mage has to have at least 1 dot in meditation for each sphere dots. So, if he wants to make up for that penalty, he has to roll meditation or use other ways to make up for it (spend quint). Or just try with the higher diff.<br /> <br /> The point is, there are drawbacks for psionics too. It isn't as easy as &quot;I think, it's done&quot; as you are saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T08:15:45-07:00","id":1520945,"title":"","content":"Late joiner to the discussion, I have doubts about the bolded part:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520943#post1520943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>To be honest, the raw is that the mage has to have at least the same amount of dots in the related ability as the Sphere of the effect.</b><br /> it is also raw that you can apply penalties for casting and distractions are on the table in M20 p506<br /> It is also raw that a mage can roll his relates ability to reduce casting difficulties.<br /> <br /> So, add everything together and in a stressful situation you apply a penalty on the Arete roll diff. <b>And the mage has to have at least 1 dot in meditation for each sphere dots. </b>So, if he wants to make up for that penalty, he has to roll meditation or use other ways to make up for it (spend quint). Or just try with the higher diff.<br /> <br /> The point is, there are drawbacks for psionics too. It isn't as easy as &quot;I think, it's done&quot; as you are saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that stated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T08:53:27-07:00","id":1520948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520945#post1520945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Late joiner to the discussion, I have doubts about the bolded part:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Where is that stated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Minimum abilities M20 p. 276. It is an optional rule, but still a rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T08:56:33-07:00","id":1520949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520945#post1520945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Late joiner to the discussion, I have doubts about the bolded part:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Where is that stated?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the Minimum Abilities optional rule in the sidebar on page 276 of the M20 core book. So that exists, at least (although, obviously, optional).<br /> <br /> But the idea that has been claimed, that rules say the ST can call for an ability roll when that ability is used to focus magick, just isn\u2019t true. I\u2019m pretty sure that\u2019s just a house rule that many groups have used for so long that they have forgotten it isn\u2019t in the rulebook; although perhaps it has been carried over from something found in an earlier edition (possibly in the core rulebook of an earlier edition, but maybe an option presented or just hinted at somewhere in the plethora of sourcebooks published over the decades).<br /> <br /> And having an ability roll you can make to reduce casting difficulties isn\u2019t a disadvantage. It\u2019s distinctly an advantage, and especially so when the ST establishes that this is an ability that can be performed for this purpose without any physical accoutrements, within a single combat round. The abilities associated with many other practices can\u2019t be used so quickly and easily for this.<br /> <br /> Which brings us back to the \u201cMage distracted\u201d modifier, which is actually on page 503 (not 506) of the M20 rule book. This now stands as the only disadvantage of meditation (and probably a few similar instruments). But this disadvantage is a single line in a table, with no related explanation anywhere I can find. There\u2019s no support for the idea that our example psion is more prone to distraction, and thus deserving of a higher \u201cMage distracted\u201d penalty, than any other type of mage. This is just the ST deliberately applying a penalty unevenly.<br /> <br /> And why is the penalty being applied unevenly? Because the ST thinks the instrument, and the Focus and character itself, are unbalanced. The ST is correct, of course, but that still means we\u2019re looking at the ST applying a house rule to patch a problem encountered when using the rules straight.<br /> <br /> And me? I\u2019d rather have a few more options in my bag of tricks. If I\u2019m going to house rule anyway (and let\u2019s face it, I always have, for decades) I might as well have a variety of house rules so that I have a better chance of being able to cobble something together that keeps everybody at the table happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T10:48:03-07:00","id":1520958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520949#post1520949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s the Minimum Abilities optional rule in the sidebar on page 276 of the M20 core book. So that exists, at least (although, obviously, optional).<br /> <br /> But the idea that has been claimed, that rules say the ST can call for an ability roll when that ability is used to focus magick, just isn\u2019t true. I\u2019m pretty sure that\u2019s just a house rule that many groups have used for so long that they have forgotten it isn\u2019t in the rulebook; although perhaps it has been carried over from something found in an earlier edition (possibly in the core rulebook of an earlier edition, but maybe an option presented or just hinted at somewhere in the plethora of sourcebooks published over the decades).<br /> <br /> And having an ability roll you can make to reduce casting difficulties isn\u2019t a disadvantage. It\u2019s distinctly an advantage, and especially so when the ST establishes that this is an ability that can be performed for this purpose without any physical accoutrements, within a single combat round. The abilities associated with many other practices can\u2019t be used so quickly and easily for this.<br /> <br /> Which brings us back to the \u201cMage distracted\u201d modifier, which is actually on page 503 (not 506) of the M20 rule book. This now stands as the only disadvantage of meditation (and probably a few similar instruments). But this disadvantage is a single line in a table, with no related explanation anywhere I can find. There\u2019s no support for the idea that our example psion is more prone to distraction, and thus deserving of a higher \u201cMage distracted\u201d penalty, than any other type of mage. This is just the ST deliberately applying a penalty unevenly.<br /> <br /> And why is the penalty being applied unevenly? Because the ST thinks the instrument, and the Focus and character itself, are unbalanced. The ST is correct, of course, but that still means we\u2019re looking at the ST applying a house rule to patch a problem encountered when using the rules straight.<br /> <br /> And me? I\u2019d rather have a few more options in my bag of tricks. If I\u2019m going to house rule anyway (and let\u2019s face it, I always have, for decades) I might as well have a variety of house rules so that I have a better chance of being able to cobble something together that keeps everybody at the table happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you really need more than that? If the mage is distracted, apply a penalty, from +1 to +3 (according to table) depending on how distracted the mage is.<br /> <br /> Yes it applies for several instruments, but not all.<br /> <br /> A Psionic is someone that uses mental power to change reality. It's only logic that it will be affected by distracting and stressful situations. <br /> <br /> <b>if the player (or you here in this thread) wants to argue that his specific Psionic is not affected by distractions, then he must provide an explanation, which includes his entire foci.</b> <br /> <br /> I see that you are more concerned about instruments balance than the instruments explanations and RP.<br /> <br /> So, I have to repeat myself, since you didn't adressed the important points I made before.<br /> <br /> 1) Psionic-like instruments (Meditation, energy, thought forms, etc.) require concentration and are prone to penalties. <br /> <br /> 2) Psionics, as many mystics effects, tend to be more vulgar. <br /> <br /> 3) And the most important: Instruments aren't balanced. Deal with it. Eye contact will never be as cumbersome as lab.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T21:46:19-07:00","id":1521009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520958#post1520958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you really need more than that? If the mage is distracted, apply a penalty, from +1 to +3 (according to table) depending on how distracted the mage is.<br /> <br /> Yes it applies for several instruments, but not all.<br /> <br /> A Psionic is someone that uses mental power to change reality. It's only logic that it will be affected by distracting and stressful situations.<br /> <br /> <b>if the player (or you here in this thread) wants to argue that his specific Psionic is not affected by distractions, then he must provide an explanation, which includes his entire foci.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lord Revan, it\u2019s become very apparent that the most verifiable claim you made about rules as written is not actually written into the rules at all. I don\u2019t believe the rest of this is either. This is all house rules. I you claim otherwise, it\u2019s up to you to establish that with clear references to the actual rules in the book. And no, I\u2019m not interested in your inferences based on the rules at this point. If you want to claim rules as written, stick with the quotes themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520958#post1520958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that you are more concerned about instruments balance than the instruments explanations and RP.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know nothing about what sort of play occurs at my table. Your comments on this matter are unwelcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1520958#post1520958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) And the most important: Instruments aren't balanced. Deal with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I intend to deal with it. However, dealing with it does not involve simply ignoring these sorts of system weaknesses until they cause a problem. I created this thread to discuss an option to help deal with this, and I now intend to stop wasting time on your arguments that I should, in fact, do nothing to deal with it and just ignore it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T07:58:54-07:00","id":1521029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1521009#post1521009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lord Revan, it\u2019s become very apparent that the most verifiable claim you made about rules as written is not actually written into the rules at all. I don\u2019t believe the rest of this is either. This is all house rules. I you claim otherwise, it\u2019s up to you to establish that with clear references to the actual rules in the book. And no, I\u2019m not interested in your inferences based on the rules at this point. If you want to claim rules as written, stick with the quotes themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this for real? Are you really trying to invalidate my arguments because I confused a little detail in raw, <b>and corrected it</b>? Dude you are the ST. You <b>can</b> ask for rolls if you want. But if you want to stick entirey on raw, I already provided a solution that you know it's raw (you even posted the right page). <br /> <br /> Also, this part you quoted never refered to raw. I really missed what is yor point here. You don't want to apply the distraction penalty either?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1521009#post1521009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know nothing about what sort of play occurs at my table. Your comments on this matter are unwelcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care if you like them or not. It is clear that you are worried about balance in instrments, which is basically fluff, in a WoD game. Good luck balancing everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1521009#post1521009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I intend to deal with it. However, dealing with it does not involve simply ignoring these sorts of system weaknesses until they cause a problem. I created this thread to discuss an option to help deal with this, and I now intend to stop wasting time on your arguments that I should, in fact, do nothing to deal with it and just ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and everyone is saying that your way to deal with it is worse than just going along with what the books already provide (not ignoring it). My argument is that you should ask the player for a good foci (which you said they did) and apply the penalties when you think they should apply. <br /> <br /> That alone will prevent that example you posted to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T09:52:25-07:00","id":1521038,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11151\" data-vbnamecard=\"11151\">travisjhall</a> Lord Revan (and others) have explained the arguments, if you don't <i>like </i>them, that is understandable; but not liking them does not make them go away nor does make them invalid.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> don't get baited into a more heated argument, you made your points and gave the reasoning behind, I advise you to stop here before this becomes uncivil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T18:40:36-07:00","id":1521089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519313-spheres-as-instruments?p=1521038#post1521038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11151\" data-vbnamecard=\"11151\">travisjhall</a> Lord Revan (and others) have explained the arguments, if you don't <i>like </i>them, that is understandable; but not liking them does not make them go away nor does make them invalid.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cI like to apply the \u2018Mage distracted\u2019 penalty more harshly on the meditation instrument to handle cases like this, and my group finds this adequate to handle the types of characters in question,\u201d is a perfectly valid argument, and helpful advice. Advice which I have noted, BTW.<br /> <br /> The commentary on how Lord Revan thinks I value roleplaying is, and always has been, uncivil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}